diff --git a/docs/development/performance-testkit.md b/docs/development/performance-testkit.md
index 299814017..417d3e3b5 100644
--- a/docs/development/performance-testkit.md
+++ b/docs/development/performance-testkit.md
@@ -651,6 +651,18 @@ Every supplemental preparation, collection, processing and cleanup phase uses th
 A failed attempt cannot donate rows to a later attempt; an unsupported whole workload is reported as a failure without substituting a subset.
 Full original JMH and applicable native/runtime Issue acceptance remain independently required.
 
+An existing owner collector keeps its original command-line and raw report contract through `owner_reports`.
+The default raw contract requires schema version 1, the declared workload identity and each phase's exact warmup/sample profile.
+A collector with an existing named contract can declare exact primitive `report_conditions`; status, independent invocation/repetition, complete rows and actual loaded runtime archives remain mandatory.
+Only an explicit `profile_location: "report"` permits phases to inherit the matching top-level profile; any phase override must still match it.
+`auxiliary_rows` declares complete separately sampled lifecycle inventories and their original sample counts without merging them into operation timing or inventing absent raw fields.
+
+An original four-argument collector additionally declares `paired_jmh` with its complete suite and compiled fixture class.
+After preparation, the driver freezes one plan containing the actual compiled fixture identity, both source ref/tree/patch bindings and runtime archive hashes, then archives that plan as an input of every matching JMH collection.
+The collector receives its own AverageTime receipt and that unchanged plan after its original output and repetition arguments.
+Its original actual executable, full JVM arguments, source/archive and complete-work checks remain responsible for rejecting a mismatched pairing.
+Owner comparison runs on its retained candidate classpath and receives the actual selected collector JAR path after verifying it against the original collector bytes.
+
 Every Gradle invocation requires fresh available physical RAM of at least 4096 MiB, checked again inside its owning Windows Job immediately before Java.
 The suspended caller is assigned before it can start Gradle; descendants inherit a 3 GiB committed-memory limit, kill-on-close and no breakaway.
 One invocation has 1800 seconds of work and 30 seconds of cleanup, one Gradle worker and one test fork.
diff --git a/docs/development/performance.md b/docs/development/performance.md
index 40b20fe97..02f9d19c8 100644
--- a/docs/development/performance.md
+++ b/docs/development/performance.md
@@ -48,6 +48,22 @@ Reviewers should compare runs made on the same controlled host and investigate s
 
 ## Deterministic structural gates
 
+### Current client editable membership
+
+The remote client state store indexes editable capability by the same current remote identity and trusted type token as its complete store.
+Admission fixes the value and adds editable membership once; preparation updates preserve membership and original insertion order.
+Distinct keys referencing one value remain distinct entries, and every current editable entry is polled even without a dirty notification.
+The index is execution-owner confined, bounded by the current store and negotiated collection limit, and contains no authoritative value snapshots.
+Retirement removes both references before invoking the entry's release callback; terminal or failed-session cleanup clears the complete index before attempting all releases.
+Close is an irreversible admission cutoff, including inside factory, update, retirement and polling callbacks.
+Entry preparation rejects callback reentry before mutation, retirement has no admission window, and a fresh factory result returned after close is released instead of retained.
+
+The native-free client-state corpus measures idle flush, local edits, pre-action flush, incoming replacements and complete address churn separately at 100, 1,000 and 8,192 current entries with none, ten or all entries editable.
+Its untimed independent map wrapper counts actual entry traversal and checks ordered edits, recursive allocation, replacement and cleanup; timed scenes use ordinary production maps.
+Shared-kit owner CPU intervals supplement JMH elapsed time and normalized allocation, with native upload and GPU scopes unavailable in this corpus.
+Each CPU report validates and hashes its exact paired JMH receipt/results, actual runtime archives, fixture tree, collector, full workload controls and actual JVM/OS/argument metadata before and after collection.
+An immutable external source plan binds both exact revisions to their archive inventories and the frozen fixture revision/tree; it is archived as the same fixture input on both sides.
+
 ### Current CycleButton selection
 
 Each retained CycleButton borrows at most one immutable live selected-value reference and its derived first matching index.
diff --git a/docs/reference/remote-protocol.md b/docs/reference/remote-protocol.md
